A Fragment allows you to return multiple elements without adding an extra HTML element such as <div>.

Using Fragment
function App() {
  return (
    <React.Fragment>
      <h1>Hello</h1>
      <p>Welcome to React</p>
    </React.Fragment>
  );
}

export default App;

You can also use the shorter syntax:
function App() {
  return (
    <>
      <h1>Hello</h1>
      <p>Welcome to React</p>
    </>
  );
}

export default App;

The <> </> syntax is commonly used